13su|n|A triangular sail set upon a stay or halyard extending from the foremast or fore-topmast to the bowsprit or the jib boom. Large vessels often carry several jibe; as, inner jib; outer jib; flying jib; etc. ; The projecting arm of a crane, from which the load is suspended. ; To move restively backward or sidewise, -- said of a horse; to balk.	N:1rn8,132,2~1rn8,132,2
